# 2️⃣ Create a Method to Check Even or Odd

### 💡 Concept
A method can return a `boolean` value: `true` or `false`.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p3;

public class MethodToCheckEvenOrOdd {

    static boolean isEven(int num) {
        return num % 2 == 0;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        boolean result = isEven(10);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
```

### ▶️ Output

```text
true
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
num = 10

10 % 2 = 0

0 == 0
   ↓
true
```

### 🧠 Important Points

```java
num % 2 == 0
```

means the number is even.

### ⚡ Tip & Trick

For a boolean method, you can often directly return the condition:

```java
return condition;
```

Instead of:

```java
boolean result = false;

if(condition) {
    result = true;
}

return result;
```

### 🎯 Interview Tip
Knowing when a condition itself can be returned makes your code shorter and cleaner.

### ⏱️ Complexity
- Time: `O(1)`
- Space: `O(1)`

