# 4️⃣ Create a Method to Find the Maximum of Two Numbers

### 💻 Code

```java
package p3;

public class MethodMaxOfTwoNumbers {

    static int max(int a, int b) {

        int result;

        if(a > b) {
            result = a;
        } else {
            result = b;
        }

        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int result = max(15, 20);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
```

### ▶️ Output

```text
20
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
a = 15
b = 20

15 > 20 → false

result = 20

return 20
```

### 🧠 Important Concept — Scope

A variable's **scope** means the area where that variable can be accessed.

```java
int result;

if(a > b) {
    result = a;
}
```

`result` was declared outside the `if`, so it can still be used after the `if`.

But:

```java
if(a > b) {
    int max = a;
}

System.out.println(max); // ERROR
```

`max` was created inside the `{ }` block.

### ⚡ Tip & Trick

> `{ }` creates a boundary for variable scope.

### 🎯 Interview Tip
Scope is a very common programming concept. Always know where a variable is declared and where it can be accessed.

### ⏱️ Complexity
- Time: `O(1)`
- Space: `O(1)`

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

