# 6️⃣ Create a Method to Find the Largest of Three Numbers

### 💻 Code

```java
package p3;

public class MethodLargestOf3Num {

    static int maxOfThree(int a, int b, int c) {

        int result;

        if(a > b && a > c) {
            result = a;
        } else if(b > a && b > c) {
            result = b;
        } else {
            result = c;
        }

        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int result = maxOfThree(10, 25, 15);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
```

### ▶️ Output

```text
25
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
a = 10
b = 25
c = 15

10 > 25 && 10 > 15
false

25 > 10 && 25 > 15
true

result = 25

return 25
```

### 🧠 Important Points

`&&` means **both conditions must be true**.

```java
a > b && a > c
```

means:

> `a` must be greater than both `b` and `c`.

### ⚡ Tip & Trick

For finding the largest:

```text
Assume a is largest
Compare b
Compare c
Return largest
```

This approach becomes even more useful when the number of values increases.

### 🎯 Interview Tip
Understand the difference between:

```java
&&
```

and:

```java
||
```

`&&` → ALL conditions must be true.

`||` → AT LEAST ONE condition must be true.

### ⏱️ Complexity
- Time: `O(1)`
- Space: `O(1)`

