# 7️⃣ Create a Method to Calculate Sum from 1 to N

### 💻 Code

```java
package p3;

public class MethodSumof1ToN {

    static int sumN(int n) {

        int sum = 0;

        for(int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            sum = sum + i;
        }

        return sum;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int result = sumN(5);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
```

### ▶️ Output

```text
15
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
n = 5

i = 1 → sum = 1
i = 2 → sum = 3
i = 3 → sum = 6
i = 4 → sum = 10
i = 5 → sum = 15
```

### 🧠 Important Points

When the question says:

> Sum from 1 to N

use:

```java
i <= n
```

not:

```java
i < n
```

### ⚡ Tip & Trick

Remember:

```text
<  → exclude
<= → include
```

### 🎯 Interview Tip

There is also a mathematical solution:

```java
int sum = n * (n + 1) / 2;
```

This reduces the algorithm from `O(n)` to `O(1)`.

### ⏱️ Complexity
- Loop solution: `O(n)`
- Space: `O(1)`

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 8️⃣ Create a Method to Count Even Numbers from 1 to N

### 💻 Code

```java
package p3;

public class MethodCountEvenNumFrom1ToN {

    static int countEven(int n) {

        int count = 0;

        for(int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {

            if(i % 2 == 0) {
                count++;
            }
        }

        return count;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int result = countEven(10);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
```

### ▶️ Output

```text
5
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
2  → count = 1
4  → count = 2
6  → count = 3
8  → count = 4
10 → count = 5
```

### 🧠 Important Points

Even number:

```java
i % 2 == 0
```

### ⚡ Tip & Trick

You can start at `2` instead of `1` because `1` cannot be even.

### 🎯 Interview Tip

This combines three important patterns:

```text
LOOP + CONDITION + COUNTER
```

This pattern appears frequently in beginner and interview problems.

